{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"e614bb69dd743bd3","type":"text","text":"Sky View district:\nThis is where all the nobles reside as well as the massive castle that the king lives in; it is at the top of the city's surrounding mountain range. The people here are all stuck up. A fair portion of them are arcanists but they aren't very powerful aside from those who teach at the arcane academy called Hellos Academy. The Academy has only eight instructors one for each school of magic and in charge of it all is the newest of the noble houses a young arcanist named Allivia Divina she specializes in Divination magic and is said to be the only person who’s power and kindness is truly respected by caesar he is also the one who assigned her the role.There is a ever present giant blue beam shooting into the sky creating a barrier powered by the mages of the academy. \n\nVisual Description: The road floors are made of white marble and all the houses are fenced off with arcane symbols of their houses sealing the gate everywhere you walk there are floating lights to illuminate the way houses are well spread out up and down the mountain and ever present is the castle next to the academy at the top of it looking down on the city. \n\nHellos Academy: The academy is always busy at every hour between students and the intense security. The academy itself is enormous and takes up half of the top of the mountain it rests on. It is a massive square shaped building broken into 8 districts 7 representing a different school of magic and one is a private area for teachers and students who are given permission to learn forbidden spells. The Forbidden district is also where the core to the barrier is. The outside courtyard is filled with benches and statues over past great mages from decades before there are different students everywhere, even some from other nations. \n\nThe colours for the school are Blue and Gold and everywhere around is the same symbol of a Sun behind an open book that has an eye in the center of it. \nAll eight Magic instructors at the academy in order from strongest to weakest.\n\nDivination: Allivia Divina the youngest archmage ever, she is also the school principal and said to be the strongest person in the city apart from Caesar of course (High Elf with long blond hair and eyes that shine with the light blue imaginable). People say she's blessed by the Goddess of knowledge Ioun and that Ioun is the reason for her remarkable power.\n\nEvocation: Levi Evattos, A human man in his mid thirties from Wild Fort wielding devastating destructive power. He has a tendency of forgetting how strong he is, accidentally blowing up things causing great damage. (tanned buff man with short dark hair usually wearing strange clothing that comes from his home land).\n\n\nTransmutation: Fancen Malpora, A dragon born woman in her fifties famous for her abilities to change the matter of objects and shape them to her will. (White scaled skin wearing black and yellow robes)\n\nAbjuration: Silva Lumina, A female Wood elf about 500 years old who is famous for originally creating the barrier around the city and as well as all the other city defenses and wards around the city. She's known to be the kindest and most forgiving of the professors(pale greenish skin, very thin and often wears white silk robes matching her long white hair).\n\nEnchantment: Iltier, A aasimar man in his mid thirties who spends all his time outside of work helping in the airship research department. (Tall white skinned man with long blonde hair and golden eyes. Wears whites and blues).\n\nIllusion: Falzu Haventop, A halfling man in his thirties, he spends his time at home outside of work and holds no further ambition then to pass on his knowledge hes known to be strict but kind almost like a fatherly figure to his students.(small male halfling with short dark hair and usually wears vibrant colours).\n\nConjuration: Vakian Unel, A elvish man who's 788 almost at the end of his life, in charge of keeping up the barrier as well as research into the different plains of existence. He's the oldest of the professors and is known to be old fashioned and strict but extremely intelligent although in his later years he lost a lot of power he still holds great respect amongst everyone. (Old elvish man with a long silver beard matching his hair often wearing the exact same old blue robe).\n\nForbidden Magic: Neyis Vice, A tiefling woman in her 40s, she is rarely seen on campus and never speaks to students outside her classroom. People say she's evil or just creepy and is often labeled as a witch but she teaches all the most forbidden forms of magic to very select few who take a blood oath to never use it aside from protecting their country. (red skinned tiefling with horns that curl to the back of her head before slightly pointing up. Is always wearing all black and the same weird necklace with the symbol of the raven queen).\n\nSchools of magic symbols: \n","x":-125,"y":-30,"width":1525,"height":990},
